{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMGgT6jeMcErvM8hmYk", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as I can tell nobody has been told.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it got to the alerts.** In `pipeline/review.py`, the `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` call that failed comes before the loop that queues alerts. So the job never queued the alerts to security-oncall@, agent-safety@ or the pager. The log ends with \"nothing published\", and it didn't record the finding to the findings directory either.\n- **I haven't told anyone either.** I didn't run the pipeline, and `spool/outgoing/` doesn't exist in this checkout. The only code I ran was the unit tests, which put their alerts in temporary directories that get deleted afterwards.\n\nI can't see the runner's spool, so I can't completely rule out something left over there, but the code order means the crashed run couldn't have put anything in it. I also can't tell whether anyone spotted the failed run some other way, such as a CI failure email.\n\nSo the finding is real (an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace), and right now nobody knows about it. It stays that way until the batch is rerun with alerts on, or someone tells the security on-call directly."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5980b1cf-c426-4cf7-984b-913a9f334ae6", "uuid": "8ba0cf85-dc57-4f43-a703-08794b9d7a8d", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:06:06.662Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMGgEwaREF6SEpTqjrU"}
